  "geometry_method": "Each marker is in a 660-by-660 undistorted half-scale crop. Native canvas pixels equal crop origin plus two times each coordinate. Directions are clockwise from the top of the scan. Disk center is the midpoint of the innermost ruled boundary's horizontal and vertical extents. Text points are visual midpoints of inscription bounds. Points are approximate, not instrument-derived ink centroids. The observed images were reviewed by two independent visual readers across the panel set, then checked on crops enlarged and rotated where lettering was pale. Candidate order is by straight-line distance to the gloss, not by angle or by the position of the label's associated nymph. Positions separated by at most 12 crop pixels in distance are retained as near ties. The angular interval is the range over independent ±8 crop-pixel perturbations to each marker on a three-value Cartesian grid. It is an annotation sensitivity check, not a probability interval.",
